From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:54:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: Balance PCI CE IRQs when cancelling interrupt
 work

The PCI CE interrupt handler disables the IRQ before queuing service
work. Normally the worker enables it again. When suspend or shutdown
cancels pending work before it can run, the interrupt remains disabled
one level too deep for the next device start to unmask it.

Pair the handler's disable with an enable when cancel_work_sync()
reports that it cancelled pending work. The enclosing suspend or
shutdown path still owns its separate mask.

Codex identified the IRQ nesting issue, implemented the cancellation
unwind and verified the mask depths with source-based tests.

Fixes: cdad73716057 ("wifi: ath12k: convert tasklet to BH workqueue for CE interrupts")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
index 3ea95d8..e77644d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -988,7 +988,9 @@ static void ath12k_pci_cancel_workqueue(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 		if (ath12k_ce_get_attr_flags(ab, i) & CE_ATTR_DIS_INTR)
 			continue;
 
-		cancel_work_sync(&ce_pipe->intr_wq);
+		/* The interrupt handler disabled the IRQ before queuing this work. */
+		if (cancel_work_sync(&ce_pipe->intr_wq))
+			enable_irq(ab->irq_num[ATH12K_PCI_IRQ_CE0_OFFSET + i]);
 	}
 }
 
